    "title": "NBA selects Spurs' Mitch Johnson as coach of the year finalist",
    "text": "San Antonio Spurs head coach Mitch Johnson, left, talks to Spurs guard Devin Vassell (24) during the second half of an NBA basketball game against the Chicago Bulls in Chicago, Monday, Jan. 6, 2025. (AP Photo/Nam Y. Huh)Nam Y. Huh/Associated PressThe NBA on Sunday announced the Spurs' Mitch Johnson as one of three finalists for its coach of the year award.Johnson's selection thrilled a player who worked closely with him long before the Seattle native and former Spurs assistant succeeded Gregg Popovich, the NBA's all-time winningest coach and a five-time league champion.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢\"Tremendously happy for him,\" forward Devin Vassell said before Game 1 of the Spurs' first-round playoff series with Portland.\"He was my guy, my personal development guy. So to see the growth he's had, to see where he is at now, to be able to come in after a coach like coach Pop, one of the greatest coaches of all time, if not the greatest coach of all time, and have the type of season he's had and be able to lead us and take control over this team and over this organization has been huge to see.\"Johnson led the Spurs to a 62-20 record in the regular season after the team named him head coach in May when Popovich retired from coaching. The Spurs finished 34-48 with Johnson as their acting head coach in 2024-25 after Popovich suffered a stroke five games into the season.\"It just shows how much work and how much trust the organization and the players have in him,\" Vassell said. \"I think he should win coach of the year. It's just been an amazing year and we're just getting started.\"Article continues below this adThe other finalists for the Red Auerbach Trophy are Detroit's J.B. Bickerstaff and Boston's Joe Mazzulla. San Antonio Express News LogoTake your fandom to the next level with breaking news, in-depth reports and expert analysis.",
